      "question": "What is the comparison of revenue level and day-to-day jitter between Sports and Books over Q1?",
      "question_style": "natural_language",
      "ground_truth": {
        "task_type": "vague_multi",
        "answer": {
          "type": "open_ended",
          "value": "Sports runs an order of magnitude above Books on revenue in that quarter—roughly a four-hundred-ish mean daily ticket versus mid-sixties for Books—so the Sports line rides much higher on the y-axis. Both still wiggle day to day, but Books stays in a narrower band while Sports shows wider swings, including occasional spikes toward the upper hundreds or nearly two thousand on strong days."
        },
        "key_insights": [
          "Sports dominates Books on absolute revenue throughout Q1.",
          "Sports carries almost all of the visible volatility; Books looks comparatively flat."
